Usage: agent-deck telemetry <command> [--json]

Opt-in, anonymous usage telemetry. OFF by default; nothing is sent until you
explicitly say yes. Full details: https://github.com/asheshgoplani/agent-deck/blob/main/TELEMETRY.md

Commands:
  status      Show consent, install id, endpoint, last send day, pending counters
  enable      Show the disclosure and require an interactive answer (y/N).
  disable     Turn telemetry off, delete the install id and pending counters
  preview     Print the exact current candidate JSON body without sending
  show-last   Print the exact JSON body of the last report sent
  reset-id    Replace the random install id with a new one

Flags:
  --json      Machine-readable output for every command
  --yes, -y   unsupported: explicit interactive consent is required (refused
              inside an agent-deck session or in CI: consent must come from a person)

Kill switches (win over stored consent, re-read on every run):
  AGENTDECK_TELEMETRY=0       hard off (any value other than 1/true/yes/on; =1 does NOT enable)
  DO_NOT_TRACK=1              hard off
  [telemetry] disabled=true   hard off, in config.toml
  [telemetry] endpoint=URL    self-host the receiver (https, or http to localhost)

When a report is sent:
  At most one HTTPS POST per UTC day, only from the interactive TUI (never from
  CLI commands, CI, scripts, or inside an agent-deck session). CLI commands only
  update local counters. Failures are silent and not retried until the next day.

Payload schema v1 (exactly these keys, nothing else):
  schema_version  int     1
  install_id      string  random 32 hex chars, rotatable, deleted on disable
  version         string  agent-deck version
  os, arch        string  e.g. darwin / arm64
  day             string  YYYY-MM-DD (UTC); no finer timestamp anywhere
  counters        object  integer counts, only these keys:
                          cli_invocations
                          conductor_used
                          remote_used
                          sessions_started.aider
                          sessions_started.claude
                          sessions_started.codex
                          sessions_started.copilot
                          sessions_started.crush
                          sessions_started.cursor
                          sessions_started.deepseek
                          sessions_started.gemini
                          sessions_started.hermes
                          sessions_started.opencode
                          sessions_started.other
                          sessions_started.pi
                          sessions_started.shell
                          tui_launches

Never sent: session titles, prompts, paths, commands, hostnames, usernames,
custom tool names, model names, MCP names, IP fields. Receiver operators must disable IP/access logging.

Default endpoint: https://telemetry.agent-deck.invalid/v1/ping
Current endpoint: https://telemetry.agent-deck.invalid/v1/ping
